// Title: PUA - 3Proxy Execution
// Sigma ID: f38a82d2-fba3-4781-b549-525efbec8506
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-09-13 | Modified: 2023-02-21
// ATT&CK: command-and-control, T1572
// Description: Detects the use of 3proxy, a tiny free proxy server
// False positives:
//   - Administrative activity
// References:
//   - https://github.com/3proxy/3proxy
//   - https://blog.talosintelligence.com/2022/09/lazarus-three-rats.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_pua_3proxy_execution.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\3proxy.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoFileDescription =~ "3proxy - tiny proxy server" or ProcessCommandLine contains ".exe -i127.0.0.1 -p"
